  "description": "Fresh set: written after both the rules and the prompt were final, by someone who had seen which dev and holdout phrasings the rules fail on, and run exactly once, with no change to any parser afterwards. It exists because the holdout set stopped being untouched (validate.ts's bracket check came from a holdout failure). Same instruments, prices and conventions as dev.json and holdout.json.",
  "conventions": [
    "Prices and quantities are display units, as a person writes them (BTC in coins).",
    "No price and no 'market' means a market order: the proposal says 'at market' and warns.",
    "timeInForce is only given when the text states it. Limit and stop-limit orders default to GTC; market and stop orders have none.",
    "A cancel names a symbol and side only if the text does; null means all.",
    "unclear: no quantity or a vague one, money instead of a quantity, two orders, an unknown instrument, a question or chat, invalid numbers (fractions of a share, off the tick, below the lot, zero, negative), contradictions, an iceberg with IOC/FOK, a bracket (an entry with its stop loss)."
  ],
